# Nothing here belongs in a build context. No build context in the repo excluded `.env` before
# this file existed, so a stray `.env`/`.env.secrets` could be COPY'd straight into an image.
#
# EVERY pattern is `**/`-prefixed, and that is not decoration. A bare `__pycache__/` or `*.key`
# matches only at the CONTEXT ROOT — docker does not apply it recursively. Measured: with the
# unprefixed form, `sub/__pycache__/nested.pyc` and `sub/secrets/leaked.key` were both copied into
# the image while the root-level equivalents were excluded. So the file read as a secret-leak guard
# while protecting only the one directory a secret is least likely to be hiding in, and 42 stale
# `.pyc` from the developer's machine were baked into every backend image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.venv/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.sqlite
**/*.db
**/.DS_Store
